/*
 * Unit test of x86enc.c (encoder byte tests):
 *   - every row of the table below: t1_x86_emit produces exactly the bytes
 *     GNU as produced for the Intel-syntax line in the comment (generated by
 *     tests/tier1/x86enc_expect.py), and t1_x86_decode recovers the op,
 *     the length and the memory operand;
 *   - every op id of T1_X86_OPS occurs in the table;
 *   - the info table: expanded condition names against the "<cc>"
 *     patterns, condition flag reads, implicit operands;
 *   - out-of-range operands, RSP as index, a CL operand not in RCX and a
 *     full buffer fail the emit; rel32 fixups patch correctly;
 *   - the length decoder rejects non-canonical encodings of accepted
 *     instructions and random byte strings it cannot reproduce;
 *   - x86sse.c: every encoding decodes as T1_X86_SSE with its length and
 *     R14 memory operand, its truncations do not, and out-of-range
 *     registers or counts fail the emit.
 */
